---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SupportArticle from "../../components/infopages/SupportArticle.astro";
---
<BaseLayout>
  <SupportArticle path="/support/add-from-a-store" title="Add a product from a store's website or app" intro="Looking at a product online? Send it straight to BeautyMark with the iPhone's Share button. 🛍️">

    <h2>From Safari</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the product's page, for example on sephora.com, ulta.com or a brand's own site.</li>
      <li>If the product comes in shades, <strong>pick your shade on the page first</strong>, so the right shade and photo come through.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Share</strong> (the square with an arrow pointing up) and choose <strong>BeautyMark</strong>.</li>
      <li>BeautyMark opens <strong>Add Product</strong> with the brand, name, shade, photo and link filled in. Check it over and tap <strong>Save</strong> (the ✓ on iOS 26 and later).</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>From a store's app</h2>
    <p> In the Sephora, Ulta, Target or Amazon app, open the product and tap the app's share button, then choose <strong>BeautyMark</strong>. It works the same way as Safari.
    </p>

    <h2>Don't see BeautyMark in the share sheet?</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>In the row of app icons, swipe all the way to the end and tap <strong>More</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Edit</strong>, then add <strong>BeautyMark</strong> to your favorites (or turn it on), and tap <strong>Done</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>It'll show up in the share sheet from then on.</p>

    <h2>Something didn't come through right?</h2>
    <p> Every website is set up a little differently. Sephora, Ulta, Target, Amazon, Walmart, Nordstrom, Olive Young, YesStyle, Soko Glam and most brand shops work well. On other sites BeautyMark fills in what the page offers. You can always fix the brand or name on the Add Product screen before saving. Tapping either one opens <a href="/support/find-a-product">Find your product</a>.
    </p>
  </SupportArticle>
</BaseLayout>
